>  <SELECTION_REASON>
Interactively reviewed graph. Mn–N–O 176.15°, N–O 1.18023 Å, g-xTB N–O WBO 1.7305. The closed-shell assignment for this near-linear terminal ligand is N≡[O+], with metal formal charge +1 and total charge +1. Corresponds to compound 5 of the same perchlorate salt. The authors use ν(CO)/ν(NO) and oxidation behaviour to support low-spin Mn(II)/NO•. The graph instead assigns Mn(I)/NO⁺. Localized 18 aromatic-ring bonds using WBOs and original bond lengths. The atom order and coordinates of all 49 atoms agree between XYZ and SDF. Lengths of 49 nonmetal covalent bonds: 48 within range, 0 outside range and 1 with sparse controls. Use the supplied Lewis representation for scoring; Independent evidence for the complete graph is limited.

